{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789316842,"nonce":"8nklCv5CoFm977mi7u699m+T2ug=","title":"call_method_on runs a method without its defining class","message":"VM::call_method_on (the C API's wrenCall, and every embedder call) passed\nNone as the defining class to call_closure_sync, so a static field read\ninside the method answered null and a write went nowhere: with\n`static count { __count }` and `static count=(v) { __count = v }`, a\nsetter reached through a call handle did nothing and the getter read\nnull, while the same calls from Wren code worked. The dispatcher passes\nthe class the method was found on; call_method_on now does the same, for\nan instance method the receiver's class and for a static the class\nitself. Test: capi::tests::test_call_reaches_static_fields.","files":null}]}